{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Mu4dz9zGCZrBYgXJpQnDG9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a Dream simulation of their IRT person-fit contamination detection paper targeting EMNLP 2026. I need to analyze the existing experimental data, the paper framing, and the ongoing experiments to define realistic scenarios.\n\nLet me analyze the current state:\n\n**Completed experiments with strong results:**\n- Simulation: MMLU power@15% = 97.9%, two-sided power >93% all levels\n- Controlled contamination (Qwen): |d|=3.42 at 15%, memorization fraction 0.38\n\n\n- Cross-family results (Llama) showing |d|=2.95 at 15% and |d|=3.31 at 50% with similar memorization patterns, plus lz* demonstrating 8× stronger effect sizes compared to traditional Guttman/U3 baselines\n- 4PL model ablation yielding 14-27 percentage point power improvements over 3PL, and empirical null distributions are well-calibrated across large benchmarks\n\nI'm tracking several experiments in flight: expanding the seed count from 3 to 10, running the post-RL GRPO experiment, preparing Mistral as a third model family, and planning broader controlled contamination across additional models.\n\nThe critical question is whether lz* maintains detection power after GRPO fine-tuning—that's the direct response to Wang et al. (2025). I'm also uncertain whether the cross-family consistency will hold with Mistral, and whether the effect sizes stay robust when I increase to n=10 seeds. With the ARR deadline in 4 days, I'm looking at best-case (all three experiments confirm the claims), median-case (post-RL shows degraded but still detectable signal, or Mistral shows weaker effects), and worse-case scenarios.\n\nIn the worst case, post-RL detection fails entirely, Mistral doesn't replicate, and n=10 reveals the n=3 results were high-variance flukes. The core SFT-only detection claim survives, but the RL-robustness and generalizability claims collapse. I'm tracking Cohen's d across families (Qwen at 3.42, Llama at 2.95), post-RL detection power, how many families hit |d|>2.0, memorization fraction consistency, and whether effect sizes hold stable with more seeds.\n\nNow I'm setting up the YAML config and thinking through the key unknowns: whether n=10 seeds will shift the point estimates and expose n=3 as a lucky draw, whether lz* retains any detection power post-GRPO (the biggest risk since prior MIA methods fail completely there), and whether Mistral's Cohen's d crosses the |d|>2.0 threshold to confirm cross-family consistency.\n\nI'm defining success tiers based on these outcomes. The best case is if post-RL detection survives with |d|>1.5, Mistral shows strong effect sizes with memorization fractions in the 30-40% range, and the n=10 seeds hold steady—that would make RL-robustness the headline differentiator and position this as the only binary-only method with empirical RL resilience. The median tier covers degraded but still detectable post-RL performance or partial support across families.\n\nThe worst case is if post-RL detection collapses entirely, Mistral shows weak or inconsistent results, and the seed variance is high—though the core SFT detection on existing Qwen and Llama data would remain solid, I'd need to reframe RL-robustness as preliminary evidence or defer it to future work.\n\nIf that happens, I can still position this as a principled minimal-information framework for SFT contamination with a characterization of detection boundaries, treating the RL limitations as a negative result that contributes to understanding where the method breaks down. That's still viable for EMNLP with honest scoping.\n\nNow I'm working through the specific metric ranges to nail down what the best-case effect sizes would look like across different contamination levels and model families. Looking at the median and worst-case scenarios across these model families, I'm seeing the memorization fraction spreads widen considerably in the worst case—over 15 percentage points—and the effect sizes become much more inconsistent, with only 1-2 families showing Cohen's d above 2.0. The θ-fixed approach also seems to struggle with maintaining monotonicity in the worst-case conditions, which suggests the method's robustness varies significantly depending on the setup.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering whether the n=3 estimates were inflated. The Qwen n=3 result of d=-3.42 with std=1.41 has a wide confidence interval, so the true effect could be closer to 2.5. Adding more seeds with n=10 would narrow that estimate, though it won't change the underlying population effect—just refine our precision around it. The real question is whether the clean distribution's standard deviation shifts meaningfully as I sample more seeds. I should move forward with building out the YAML configuration now, keeping track of the key assumptions as I go.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23386,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23386},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05152f0c-c626-43c7-80eb-973be7aa6f99","uuid":"e25c3805-f163-4a45-a441-8ae4d6acf1fb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Mu4dz9zGCZrBYgXJpQnDG9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"所有在进行实验按预期收敛：post-RL 保持检测力，第三家族确认一致性，n=10 seeds 收紧 CI 且效应量稳健\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"post-RL (GRPO) 后 lz* 仍可检测污染 (|d|>1.5)，验证 binary-pattern 对 RL distributional shift 的结构性免疫\"\n      - \"Mistral 第三家族 |d|>2.0，memorization fraction 落在 30-40% 区间，确认跨家族一致性\"\n      - \"n=10 seeds 扩展后 Qwen/Llama 效应量保持 |d|>2.5，CI 收窄至 ±0.5 以内\"\n      - \"θ-fixed 在所有家族均恢复/增强单调剂量响应\"\n      - \"R²=0.65 power function 在第三家族数据加入后提升至 >0.70\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cohens_d_qwen_15pct_n10: [2.5, 4.0]\n      cohens_d_llama_15pct_n10: [2.0, 3.5]\n      cohens_d_mistral_15pct: [2.0, 4.0]\n      cohens_d_post_rl_15pct: [1.5, 3.0]\n      memorization_fraction_range: [0.30, 0.42]\n      memorization_fraction_cross_family_spread_pp: [0, 5]\n      families_with_d_gt_2: 3\n      theta_fixed_monotonic_families: 3\n      item_level_auroc_all_methods: [0.50, 0.65]\n      power_function_R2_updated: [0.70, 0.85]\n      n10_ci_half_width: [0.3, 0.5]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 完全成立。三条 Claims 无需调整。\n      Headline: \"IRT-FIT 在 3 个模型家族检测 SFT 污染 |d|>2.0，且是唯一具有 post-RL 经验证据的 binary-only 方法。\"\n      Post-RL 成为最强差异化卖点——直接回应 Wang et al. (2025)，所有 MIA 方法 post-RL ≈ random 而 IRT-FIT 保持检测力。\n      三家族 + n=10 CI 构成 robustness 叙事核心。θ-fixed 通用性升级为方法论贡献。\n      投稿策略：EMNLP 2026 ARR，若错过 5/25 则瞄准后续 cycle 或 AAAI 2027。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"核心 SFT 检测稳健，但 post-RL 结果模糊或 Mistral 效果偏弱；需要调整 claims 强度和叙事重心\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"post-RL 检测力退化但未完全消失 (|d| 0.5-1.5)，或 GRPO 实验未在 deadline 前完成只有初步结果\"\n      - \"Mistral 第三家族效应量偏弱 (|d| 1.0-2.0) 或 memorization fraction 偏离 (25-30% 或 >42%)\"\n      - \"n=10 seeds 揭示 n=3 估计略有膨胀，效应量下降 20-30% 但仍显著\"\n      - \"θ-fixed 在 2/3 家族有效，第三家族表现不一致（如 Qwen 式非单调未完全修复）\"\n      - \"R²=0.65 power function 加入新数据后无改善或略降\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cohens_d_qwen_15pct_n10: [1.5, 2.5]\n      cohens_d_llama_15pct_n10: [1.5, 2.5]\n      cohens_d_mistral_15pct: [1.0, 2.5]\n      cohens_d_post_rl_15pct: [0.5, 1.5]\n      memorization_fraction_range: [0.25, 0.45]\n      memorization_fraction_cross_family_spread_pp: [5, 12]\n      families_with_d_gt_2: 2\n      theta_fixed_monotonic_families: 2\n      item_level_auroc_all_methods: [0.50, 0.65]\n      power_function_R2_updated: [0.55, 0.70]\n      n10_ci_half_width: [0.5, 0.9]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claim 1 核心成立但需软化措辞——\"cross-family detection\" 限定为 2/3 families 强效 + 1 family moderate。\n      Claim 2 不变（simulation + power function 已完成，不受新实验影响）。\n      Claim 3 中 post-RL 从 \"structural immunity\" 降级为 \"preliminary evidence of partial retention\"，\n      移入 §5.4 exploratory analysis 而非主 claim。\n      θ-fixed 从 \"universal mechanism\" 改为 \"model-dependent boundary condition\"（已有的 Qwen vs Llama 差异叙事可支撑）。\n      Memorization fraction 跨家族一致性降级为 \"approximate consistency with model-dependent variation\"。\n      补偿策略：强化 item-level near-random finding（已完成，不受影响）+ 8× effect size vs Guttman（已完成）作为独立贡献。\n      投稿策略：可投 EMNLP 但需精心控制 claims scope；AAAI 2027 是更安全选项（多 10 周完善）。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"post-RL 完全失效，第三家族不一致，n=10 暴露高方差——核心 SFT 检测仍成立但泛化性叙事瓦解，需 reframe\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"post-RL 后 lz* 检测力消失 (|d|<0.5)，与 MIA 方法一样对 RL 脆弱\"\n      - \"Mistral 第三家族 |d|<1.0 或方向不一致，跨家族一致性仅 2/3（Qwen+Llama）\"\n      - \"n=10 seeds 显示 clean lz* 分布方差大，部分 seed 效应量 <1.0，n=3 结果为幸运抽样上界\"\n      - \"θ-fixed 在 Mistral 上不恢复单调性，机制通用性不成立\"\n      - \"memorization fraction 跨家族 spread >15pp，一致性叙事不可信\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cohens_d_qwen_15pct_n10: [0.8, 2.0]\n      cohens_d_llama_15pct_n10: [0.8, 2.0]\n      cohens_d_mistral_15pct: [0.0, 1.5]\n      cohens_d_post_rl_15pct: [0.0, 0.5]\n      memorization_fraction_range: [0.15, 0.50]\n      memorization_fraction_cross_family_spread_pp: [12, 25]\n      families_with_d_gt_2: [1, 2]\n      theta_fixed_monotonic_families: [1, 2]\n      item_level_auroc_all_methods: [0.50, 0.65]\n      power_function_R2_updated: [0.40, 0.60]\n      n10_ci_half_width: [0.8, 1.5]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Reframe 方向：从 \"robust cross-family detection framework\" 转为 \"characterization of the\n      minimal-information detection frontier\"——论文核心变为系统性地刻画 binary-only 检测的能力边界和失败模式。\n      \n      新 Claim 1: \"IRT person-fit 在 SFT 污染场景下提供可检测信号（2/3 families |d|>2），但检测力对模型家族、\n      训练方法（SFT vs RL）高度敏感——这种敏感性本身是对 contamination detection frontier 的贡献。\"\n      \n      新 Claim 2 (不变): simulation + power function + 4PL ablation 全部已完成且独立于新实验。\n      \n      新 Claim 3: post-RL 失效 reframe 为 \"honest negative result\"——\"binary response patterns 在 RL 后\n      不足以检测污染，这与 Wang et al. 的 token-level findings 形成统一图景：RL 从 token 和 response 两个层级\n      同时抹除污染信号。这划定了 detection frontier 的下界。\"\n      \n      补偿资产（不受 worst case 影响）：\n      (a) universal 4PL misfit finding (57/60 flagged) — 独立贡献\n      (b) 4PL vs 3PL ablation (+14-27pp) — 独立贡献  \n      (c) item-level near-random + model-level aggregation insight — 独立贡献\n      (d) empirical null calibration analysis — 独立贡献\n      (e) 8× effect size vs classical person-fit — 已完成\n      \n      这 5 项已完成的独立贡献足以支撑一篇 EMNLP methodology paper，即使泛化性叙事弱化。\n      投稿策略：仍可投 EMNLP/AAAI，但标题从 \"IRT-FIT: Detecting Contamination...\" 改为\n      \"What Can Binary Response Patterns Reveal About Benchmark Contamination?\"——问句标题\n      暗示 characterization 而非 solution，为混合结果留空间。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23386,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23386},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05152f0c-c626-43c7-80eb-973be7aa6f99","uuid":"0417d0e9-9147-4e9b-9e00-dcff9889ce10"}
